Parameter values defined as enums (such as PARTSTAT, STATUS and TRANSP) can now be looked up case-insensitively when calling the enum directly, for example ``PARTSTAT("needs-action")`` returns ``PARTSTAT.NEEDS_ACTION``. This follows RFC 5545 section 3.1, which treats these unquoted values as case-insensitive. The canonical spelling of the values is unchanged. I used AI to assist me with this change. @Mubashir78
